==== Post-quantum cryptography

Goal: develop public-key cryptographic algorithms secure against quantum computers

broken:RSA, ECC(Elliptic curve cryptography)

against quantum computers:lattice^based system, McEliece, Some isogeny-based systems

==== NIST competitionf or post^quantum cryptosystems

Goal:replace currently cryptosystems with quatum-secure ones.

November 2017 : 69 submission avvepted in round one

2017:8 submission broken

2019:26 broken....

2022: SIKE was 4th candidate of four standard candidates

25日後: SIKE was broken

==== Elliptic curves and cryptography

ECC: start in 1985, based on hardnes of discrete log problem on elliptic curves, broken by Shor's quantum algorithm for discrete lot ('94)

object: elliptic curve defined over finite field


$
  E:y^2=x^3+ a x + b quad (a,b in FF_q)
$

isogency: $phi:E_1->E_2 $ preserves certain structuers, (homomorphism)

NIST submission, SIKE-SIDH was broken

Other isogency-based system(CSIDH, SCALLOP,...) remains secure

==== Isogency Crypto Pros/Cons
Pros:
Pool of potential post-quantum candidates is very small. Need to investigate all candidates in case one becomes insecure

Elliptic curves used in crypto for more than 20 years. Hacea alot of infranstructure in place.

Some computational assumption hace been studeied classically.


Cons:Onceo f the main system, SIDH was broken

Doew thislower confidence in other isogency-based systems?

Compared to latti...

==== The isogency Problem

$
  E_1:y^2=x~3+x\

  E_2:y^2=x^3-4x\

  phi:(x,y)|->((x^2+1)/x, (y(x^2+1)/x^2))
$

Problem:Given $E_1,E_2$, find $phi$

Pathfinding proglem for graphis: Given graph, two vertices, find path

Conside the case of supersingluar $l$-isogency graph in char $p$


Properties of $G_l$:
$G$ is exponentially large

have implicit description fo $G$

....

==== Definiing isogency graphs

$p$:large orime $l$:small prime

$G_l$:exponentially large, $tilde p/12$ vertices

Gicen a vertex, can efficiently compute neighbors

Hrd:compute path from $E$ to $E'$
==== The $l$-isogency pathfinding problem


計算量について：Delfs-Galbraith, 2016

