==== finite dim linear algebra

start with a finite dim C-algebra A

Goal:understand a c via  matrices

Take C-Basis $v_1,....,v_n$

For $a in A$, get scalars $beta_(i,j)^a eq.not gamma_(i,j)^a in CC$ s.t.
$
  v_i a = sum_(j=1)^n beta_(i,j)^a v_j eq.not a v_i =sum_(j=1)-n gamma_(j,i)^a v_j
$

get C-linear main-parts
$
  beta:A->"Mat"_n (CC), space a|->(beta_(i,j)^a)_(i,j=1)^n eq.not gamma:A->"Mat"_n (CC), space a|->(gamma_(i,j)^a)_(i,j=1)^n
$

#qu()[
  When does $exists P in "GL"_n (CC)$ s.t.
  $
    P beta(a)=gamma(a)P forall a in A
  $?
]
#ans()[
  $exists lambda in CC^n$ s.t. $P:=P_lambda^A$ is integrable
]

#def()[
  finite dim C-alg $A$ is Frobenius $<==>$ $exists lambda in CC^n$ s.t. $det(P_lambda^A) eq.not 0$
]

#eg()[
