==== How to represent 4 mfd?

From knot to 4mfd via 3mfds

#thm()[
  Lickorish-Walleve thm 1960 Every closed ori 3mfd can be obtained by surgery on framed link in $S^3$
]

determined by integers $lambda="lk"(K,K')$

framed link $(L,lambda)$, cpt 4mfd whose bdy is surgery $S_lambda^3(L)$

This is called the trace of the surgery and is denoted $X_lambda (L)$

If $S_lambda^3 (L)=S^3$, we can fill in $X_lambda (L)$ with $D^4$ and get closed 4-mfd

Handle decompositions:BY morse theory, every sm mfd is made of some basic obj called $k$-handles ( copies of $D^k times D^(n-k) $ attached along $delta D^k times D^(n-k)$)

torusを盾において、下から撮ってくと0^hundleからn^-hundleまで出てくる

closed 4mfd, 1handle, 2-handleさえ書けば、特定できる。Kirby diagramと呼ぶ。

many simply connected 4mfd can be represented without 1,3-handle, we just need to draw framed link for 2-handle


#eg()[
