==== Local and global Langlands conjectures(s) over over function fields

Statement of classical Langlands conj/thm: We will work with algebro-geometric obj over $overline(FF_q)$, the algebraic closure of finite field $FF_q$ but we will assume that obj involuted are defined over $FF_q$, so that they carry an action of the Frobenius.

Thus, we let $X$ be smooth and complete cureve and $F$ reductive gp

Our basic obj of study is
$
  "Bun"_G
$
:moduli sp of pri $G$-bdl on$X$

clasical unramified Langlands theory studies  the space
$
  "Funct"_c("Bun"_G (FF_q),QQ)
$
of compactly(=finitely) supported $QQ$-valued functions on this set.

This space is function field counterpart of the classically studied space of automophic functions, which are functions on the double quotient...


main reason:on e thing we would like to do is to finide inside (1) eigenspaces of Hecke operators

