  sigma:pi_1 (X)^"arithm"->C
$

up to conjugacy

$G$ is Langlands-dual gp, which is constructed out of $G$ completely combinatorially

A stone age conjecture would sya that Autom splits as a direct sum of copies of $overline(QQ_l)$ indexed by these $sigma$'s

Such conj is false even in simplest case of $G$ being the multiplicative gp and curve $X$ being $PP^1$


The space Autom is the space of compactly supported functions on $ZZ$, while  the direct sum would be over points of$(overline(QQ_l)^times)$, which suspiciously looks like the set of$overline(QQ_l)$-points of $GG_m$...


