Marstrand's projection theorem(1953):$E subset RR^2$:Borerl set. For almost every $theta in SS^1$,
$
  dim_H P_theta (E) = min{dim_H E, 1}
$

#thm()[
  Orponen-Shmerkin, Ren-W2023

  $E subset RR^2, Lambda subset SS^1$:Borel set

  $
    dim_H Lambda>0
  $

  E $theta in Lambda$

  $
    dim_H P_theta (E) >= min{dim_H E, (dim_ E + dim_H Lambda)/2,1}
  $
]


This proves Oberlin's conjecture(2012) as special case of Furstenberg sets conjecture


#rem()[
