]

that conjugate $cal(F)_lambda$ to $cal(F)_lambda_0$


Goal:understand moduli sp of cpx alg fol possess a non-triv dichotomy
$
  cal(M)="Stab" union.sq "Bif"
$

The ubiquity of bifurcation:"Nature proceeds by crises..."

with sufficiently ample canonical bdle such as moduli sp of degree >=2
 fol on $PP^2$ bifurcations always occur persistently

 #thm()[
   The bifurcation locus has non-empty interior
]


The persistent mechanism responsible for bifurcations in these moduli spaces is the local density of the holonomy pserudo-group: any germ of biholomorphism between transverse sections is a uniform limit of holonomuy maps on a fixed domain.

This implies ergodicity, minimality and local rigidity

The proof for the local density of the holonomy pseudogroup is built upon ingenious renormalization procedures-originating with the foundational 1960s work of Khudai-Verenov and Ilyashenko and culminating in Loray and Rebelo's breakthrough

Hudaj-Verenov1962->...


#conj()[
  $
    overline({lambda in Lambda : cal(F)_lambda ...})attach(=, b:?) "Bif"
  $
]



#conj()[
  foliation exhibiting holonomy maps with parabolic fixed points are dense in moduli spaces with sufficiently ample canonical bundle
]


This density phenomenon is fully understood in moduli spaces of rational maps and of keinian groups, by the foundational work of Marie, Sad, Sullivan,...


#def()[
  Riccati foliation on alg surf is fol which is trans to generic fibre of fibration by ra curve over certain base curve
]

In suitable birat coord where ruling is given by $z$, Riccati fol is defined by
$
  (d x)/(d z) = A (z) x^2 +B(z) x + C(z)
$
where $A,B$ and $C$ are rat fcn in $z$

$
  z(1-z) y'' +[c-(a+b+1)z]y'-a b y=0\
  a=(1+delta)/2, b=(1-delta)/2, c=1-delta, quad delta in CC
$

#conj()[
  In moduli spaces offoliations with sufficiently ample canonical bundle on non-ruled surfaces, the bifurcation locus is entire moduli space
]

