#thm()[
  conv thm for 2D and 3D Ricci flow

  $dim M=3$ $g_0$: has pos Ricci curvature
  Then, Ricci flow exists up to some finite time $T$ As $t->T$, mfd collapses to pt and becomes round after suitable rescaling. In particular, $M$ admits metric of const curv and $M$ is diffeo to quotient of $S^3$ by std isometries
]

#thm()[
  Hamilton1989 Chow1991

  $g_0$:initial metric on $S^2$

  Then, Ricci flow exists up to some finite time $T$

  As $t->T$ , mfd collapse to pt. and becomes round after suitable rescaling. Ricci flow be dfrom $g_0$ to const curv met and conf str is unchanged under evolution
]



