=== Critical long-range percolation

Phase transitions: When small change in microscopic para engenders abrupt change in macroscopic behaviour of system


e.g.  Kettle, Three^phase traffic theory

many phase transitions very poorly understood theoretically

criticality (the point where phase transition occurs), many systems exhibit remarkable fractal behaviour

reasonably well understood in 2 dimensions and high dimensions, very poorly understood inbetween

Some key words:Scale invariane, power laws, emergent symmetries universality

Every edge of graph $G$ is deleted or retained independetly with retention probability $p$

Retained edgesare open, deleted edges are closed.

Open connected components are clusters

critical probability $rho_c (G) = inf { p in [0,1] : "infinite clusters exist"}$

There is phase transition: In dim $d>1, 0<p_c <1$

For square grid $p_c=1/2$ (Kesten 1980)

#conj()[
  No percolation at $p_c$ in any dim abocve 1. Open for $ 3 =< d =<6$


]

