Dirichlet proglem:Given $Omega subset RR^(n+1), space f: partial Omega->RR, space f in C (partial Omega)$, find $u in C(overline(Omega)) inter C^2 (Omega)$ s.t.

$
  cases(Delta u = sum_(i=1)^(n+1 partial_(i,i))^2 u =0 "in" Omega, u=f "in" partial Omega)
$


sol $u$  of Dirichlet prob in $Omega$ can be of harmonic measure $omega^p$

For $p in Omega$ , E prob meas supported on $partial Omega$ s.t. for $f in C(partial Omega)$

$
  u(p)=integral_(partial Omega) f(xi) d omega^p (xi)
$


So $omega^p (E) $ is value at $p$ of harmonic extension of $chi_E$ to $Omega$


If $omega$ is connected and $p_1, p_2 in Omega$, then $omega¥p_1, omega^p_2$ are mutually absolutely conti $<==> omega^p_1 g omega^p_2$ for function $g>0$

#qu()[
  When are $cal(H)^n|_(partial Omega) $ and $omega^p$ mut abs conti?

  Which is connection with recti?

]


We are interested in open set whose bdy may be rough

#thm()[
  Kakutani1944

  Let $Omega$ be open bdd

  $x_0 in Omega$

  $E subset partial Omega$

  Then $omega^x_0 (E)$ conincides with prob that Brownian motion started at $x_0$ first exits $Omega$ through $E$
]

#list(indent: 2em)[
  Riesz 'Riesz1916:If $Omega subset CC$ is simply connected and $cal(H)^1 (partial Omega)<infinity$ (in particular $partial Omega$ is 1^recti), then $cal(H)^1|_(partial Omega)$ and $omega^p$ are mut abso conti $<==> omega^p =g cal(H)^1|_(partial Omega)$ for function $g>0$
][
  False in higher dim
][
  Dahlberg1977: If $Omega subset RR^(n+1) $ is Lipschitz dom, then $cal(H)^n|_(partial Omega)$ and $omega^p$ are mut abso cont in quantitative way


]


