Riesz transform: For Borel meas $mu$ in $RR^(n+1)$ and $1 =< p < infinity$, $L^p (mu)$ is space of function $f$ s.t.
$
  norm(f)_(L^p (mu)) =(integral abs(f)^p d mu)^(1/p) <infinity
$

$
  cal(R)_(mu, epsilon) f(x)= integral_(abs(x-y)>epsilon) (x-y)/(abs(x-y)^(n+1)) f(y) d mu(y)
$


This si sing integral (typically defined as principal valuer)

$
  cal(R)_mu = cal(R)_mu 1
$


Riesz kernel is grad of fundamental sol of Laplacian, modulo const factor:


connection betweeen harmonic measure and Riesz transform:kernel of Riesz trans
$
  K(x)=x/(abs(x)^(n+1)) =c nabla cal(E) (x)
$

Green function
$
  G(x,p)= cal(E) (x-p) - integral cal(E) (x-y) d omega^p (y)
$

Therefore, for $x in Omega$

$
  c nabla_x G(x,p) = K(x-p) - integral K(x-y) d omega^p (y)=K(x-p) - cal(R) omega^p (x)
$

$
  norm(cal(R)_epsilon omega^p (x)) =< c abs(nabla_x G(x,p))+"error temr"\
  =< c (omega^p (B(x,epsilon)))/epsilon^n +"error term"
$

Naive idea : exi and finit of $integral_E (x-y)/(abs(x-y)^(n+1) ) d cal(H)^n (y)$ occurs only when E many cancellation, which forces $E$ tobe n-recifi

#thm()[
  Nazarov, T., Volberg, 2014

  Let $E subset RR^(n+1)$ s.t. $cal(H)^n (E ) <infinity$, then
  $
    E:n"rectifiable" <==> sup_(epsilon >0) abs(cal(R)_epsilon (cal(H)^n|_E)(x))<infinity "for" cal(H)^n"-a.e. "  x in E
  $

  In case when $E$ is $n$-Ahlfors regular,
  $
    E:"unif n-rectifi"<==> cal(R)_(cal(H)^n|_E) "is bdd in" L^2 (cal(H)|_E...)
   $
]

#thm()[
  Dabrowski,T.,2026

  $mu:$Borel meas in $RR^(n+1) $ wtih no point masses. Then $cal(R)_mu$ is bdd in $L^2 (mu) $ iff
  $
    mu(B(x,r)) =< C r^n "for all" x "and all" r>0
  $
  and
  $
    integral_B integral_0^(r(B)) beta_(2,mu) (x,r)^2 Theta_mu (x,r) (d r)/r d mu (x) <= C mu (B)
  $
  for any ball $B subset RR^(n+1)$
]

