== Mathematical Optimization in the Age of AI

continuous optimization: developed conceptual nonconvex optimization methods

conti opt is largely journal-oriented


no peer-reviewed conferences like ICML/NeurIPS/ICLR

SIAM jornal on Optimization

control (matrix opt, constraint, accurate & feasible sol, deterministic algo, It's okay if calc take a whil) -> ML (vector opt, No constraints, inaccurate sol is enough, stochastic algo, solve as quickly as possible, Oracle complexity is important)


1951 : Frank-Wolfe method -> DC opt & Bilevel opt -> Interior point -> conic opt -> robust opt ->polynomial opt & copositive opt -> renewed study of classical method

keyword: (proximal) gradient descent

cf. Nocedal&Wright, "Numerical Optimization" 2006 chapter 7 Large-Scale unconstrained optimization

#eg()[
  bilevel optimization has been studied since 1970s


]

cf. Maclaurin et al. '15 Pedregosa'16

cf. Franceschi et al. (ICML 2018): Pedregosa(ICML 2016); Ghadimi-Wang(arxiv 2018)

cf. Classical approach for simple bilevel problems

From bilevel to multilevel optimization -> first algorithm with convergence guarantees (NeurIPS 21)

Extending hte lower-level problem to Riemannian manifolds (NeurIPS 24) -> gradient-based methods that allow constraints at the lower level

Allowing nonsmooth lower-level funcitons (JMLR21, MP24, MOR26) -> methods that can handle nonsmooth lower-level objectives

